  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (the mean of all outcomes) is not considered by the individual. The individual does not calculate or refer to the mean of the outcomes of A (which is ~1633.33) or B (which is 2400). Instead, the reasoning centers on the comparison between 66% and 33% probabilities and the perceived gain, which suggests a focus on expected value or probability weighting, not the mean across outcomes. The decision reason’s rule — preferring the lottery with the higher mean outcome — is not reflected in the justification. The individual's reasoning is inconsistent with the rule of the decision reason. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
